  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q29-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "29",
    "prompt": "Find the smallest positive integer that can be written as the sum of three consecutive odd integers, and also as the sum of five consecutive odd integers, and also as the sum of seven consecutive odd integers.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$105$\n\nEach sum is the number of terms multiplied by its middle term, so use $\\operatorname{LCM}(3,5,7)=105$.",
      "worked": "The sum of an odd number of consecutive odd integers equals the number of terms multiplied by the middle term. Therefore, the required integer must be a common multiple of $3$, $5$ and $7$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{LCM}(3,5,7)&=3\\times5\\times7\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(3,5,7)&=105.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe three representations are\n$$\\begin{align*}105&=33+35+37\\\\105&=17+19+21+23+25\\\\105&=9+11+13+15+17+19+21.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus the smallest positive integer is $105$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 84
  },
